# Changelog

When you add user-facing fixes, features, or behavior changes, update `CHANGELOG.md` in the same change set.

- Keep **only the current version** section (replace prior notes when bumping).
- Write for **players**, not developers: this file is embedded and shown in the What’s new popup after updates.
- Prefer plain language. Avoid internal jargon (soft-pause, teardown, vnav, handlers, latches, IPC) unless players see that word in the UI.
- Use `### New` / `### Fixes`, short bullets, issue numbers when useful (`(#112)`).
- Skip pure refactors, internal renames with no user impact, chore-only edits, and debug/dev-only tooling unless asked.
